From 9f08f87918167f2bc1cf59998ab5d7842c249158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haowen1993 <39072333+haowen1993@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:26:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(art): support Simplified Chinese card art
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Scryfall has no Simplified-Chinese printings at all, so the existing
localized-art pipeline (a generated `scryfall-images.v2.<lng>.json` sidecar
mapping an English printing id to its localized sibling) has no zh entry to
produce and no way to produce one.

大学院废墟 (mtgch.com) mirrors Scryfall's CDN path layout one-for-one, so the
same printing id addresses the same art in Chinese:

  https://cards.scryfall.io/normal/front/f/2/<uuid>.jpg
  https://images.mtgch.com/zhs/normal/front/f/2/<uuid>.webp   ← 简体中文
  https://images.mtgch.com/sf/normal/front/f/2/<uuid>.webp    ← its English art

That makes zh a DERIVED art locale: no sidecar, no generated artifact, no
network request to become usable — `loadLocaleArt("zhs")` installs an empty map
and resolves synchronously, which is what flips `isLocaleArtReady` and releases
the render path from its `…:pending` cache key. The six mapped locales keep
their exact existing behaviour.

Availability is per PRINTING and is discoverable only by loading the image
(measured: ~100% for English on that host, but a printing with no Chinese run
404s), so the card-art ladder gains a real second rung. It is spliced in ahead
of the terminal `{kind: "fallback", src: null}` sentinel rather than appended —
`advanceFailedSource` walks the ladder in order, so a rung after the sentinel
would be unreachable and a missing Chinese printing would render the text
placeholder instead of the English art already in the array.

Art crops are deliberately NOT rewritten: a crop is the illustration alone and
carries no language, and its stored Scryfall URL (with its cache-buster) is the
one the browser already holds, so moving it would re-download the identical
picture on every hover preview to gain nothing.

Card-art language becomes its own preference instead of riding on the UI
language, because the two sets differ in both directions: zh has art but no UI
catalog (a full 4522-key translation is a separate change), and pl ships a UI
with no localized art. `"auto"` is the default and means "follow the UI", so an
existing install is unchanged.

Also widens the visual-pack candidate locale slot from an enumeration to a shape
check. `cardCandidateGroups` validates eagerly, so an unlisted code threw out of
the group builder into a caller's `try`/`catch` — silently disabling
localized-pack lookups for that language rather than failing visibly.

Verified: type-check clean; lint 0 errors; full frontend suite shows no new
failure against a baseline worktree at the pre-change commit (36 failures before
and after, all pre-existing).
